# Build-context hygiene for a frontend-rooted context. Both shipped images build from the
# repository root, so the root .dockerignore is what Docker consults for them and this list
# applies only when a build is invoked against this directory. Only generated, transient and
# machine-local material is listed - nothing `npm ci`, `ng build` or `ng test` reads - and
# there are no negation entries, so no later line can shadow an earlier one.

# The frontend image runs `npm ci` inside its build stage, so a host tree copied in would ship
# wrong-platform native bindings and defeat the deterministic lockfile install.
**/node_modules/

**/dist/
**/.angular/
out-tsc/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/
karma-results*
chrome-profiler-events*.json
speed-measure-plugin*.json

**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.eslintcache
.npm/

# Version-control metadata, enumerated rather than globbed so that no `.git*` wildcard can
# reach an asset under public/.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/ehthumbs.db
**/Desktop.ini

# Machine-local environment overrides and credentials. `**/.env*` closes that family at every
# depth, and it requires a basename beginning with a literal dot - so the workspace's real
# committed configuration under src/environments/ is deliberately NOT matched and the
# production build keeps every file it needs.
.env*
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.p8
*.jks
*.keystore
*.ppk
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.p8
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.ppk
